From 40d8244807a7dc2440e1b999eb3e197c1d1192b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Musichen <alex.musichen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:34:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(home): every claim on the home page names the
 command or the page that proves it

The primitives grid carried nine claims, none of them checkable: "Checkpoint & rollback" (a differentiation engine that does not exist), "Harness compatible", "Private registries", "Category registry". Its two code samples were invented as well: a plugin importing `cordis` (the package is @deepseek-ai/cordis) with `ctx.logger`, and a "blend.yml" naming agent-runtime, tool-router, checkpoint-store and web-surface.

- Eight cards now, each with its proof: a command a reader can run (npm create acrylblends@latest my-app notes, npx acrylblends upgrade --dry-run, npx acrylblends init my-app --desktop) or a page that documents it (Add a plugin, The app manifest, Data and migrations, Acryl in a Cordis app, What runs in production). The four claims without one are gone.
- The two samples are the real thing: a plugin the docs verify (Acryl mounted with ctx.router.route, imported from acrylblends) and the blank template's own blend.yaml.
- The line that said plugins "are published on cordisplugins.github.io, the sibling registry this site's own Blends pull from" is replaced by a link to the page that explains the plugin lifecycle: no Blends in the registry composes that plugin, so the claim was not one I could show.
- The features section gets an id, #primitives, so the grid can be linked to.

Also: the oldest release-notes page (0.3.0) now says where the releases without a page are - the GitHub releases list - instead of leaving the gap silent. No pages are added for 0.5.1, 0.6.0, 0.6.2, 0.6.3 and 0.6.4.
